Join $PQ$, $PR$, $PS$, $RQ$, and $RS$.
Since the circles with centers $Q$, $R$ and $S$ are all tangent to $BC$, then $QR$ and $RS$ are each parallel to $BC$ (as the centers $Q$, $R$ and $S$ are each 1 unit above $BC$).
